2. Employee Payroll and Deduction Analysis

1. Problem Statement
Create a payroll program that calculates gross salary from basic pay, allowances, overtime, and incentives, 
applies a simple deduction policy, and prints a salary statement.

2. Objectives
•	Compute gross earnings.
•	Apply deductions using conditions.
•	Display gross pay, deductions, and net pay.

3. Assumptions
•	Basic pay, allowances, overtime pay, and incentives are non-negative.
•	Gross salary is their sum.
•	Deduction is 5% of gross up to ₹30,000; above ₹30,000, deduction is 8% of gross.

4. Algorithm
1. Read salary components.
2. Validate that values are non-negative.
3. Add components to calculate gross pay.
4. Choose the deduction rate based on gross pay.
5. Subtract deduction and print the salary statement.

5. Flowchart
       (START)
          |
     Enter Salary
          |
  Calculate Gross Salary
          |
   Gross > 30000?
      /       \
    Yes        No
     |          |
  8% Deduction  5% Deduction
      \        /
   Calculate Net Salary
          |
  Print Salary Statement
          |
        (STOP)

6. Pseudocode

    BEGIN
INPUT units and previous bill
IF units <= 100, bill = units * 2
ELSE IF units <= 200, bill = 200 + (units-100)*3
ELSE, bill = 500 + (units-200)*5
ADD fixed charge and surcharge
IF bill > 1000, APPLY rebate
DISPLAY current bill
COMPARE with previous bill
DISPLAY unusual increase if bill > 1.5 * previous bill
END

7. Python Source Code

u = int(input("Enter units: "))
p = float(input("Enter previous bill: "))
b = u*2 if u <= 100 else 200+(u-100)*3 if u <= 200 else 500+(u-200)*5
b += 50 + (b+50)*0.05 - (50 if b+50 > 1000 else 0)
print("Bill:", round(b, 2), "Unusual Increase" if b > 1.5*p else "Normal Bill")

